cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite Athena and the associated battery study when using this code.
type: software
title: "Athena: code for curvature-associated battery electrode defect analysis"
authors:
  - family-names: Yan
    given-names: Yifei
  - family-names: Niu
    given-names: Kaile
  - family-names: Cai
    given-names: Lei
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Zhengxiang
  - family-names: Du
    given-names: Ke
  - family-names: Zan
    given-names: Guibin
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Fangyang
  - family-names: Meng
    given-names: Jinhao
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rainse02/Athena"
url: "https://github.com/Rainse02/Athena"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Study-specific Python code for post-segmentation analysis of material and
  structural defects in a commercial Li-MnO2 battery cell. The software covers
  winding geometry, curvature- and path-normalized defect statistics,
  spatial and axial profiles, sensitivity calculations, and segmentation
  validation metrics.
keywords:
  - electrochemical battery cell
  - electrode structural defects
  - X-ray computed tomography
  - winding curvature
  - spatial statistics
